@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile Plan
+
+Status: implemented (see `docs/capability_status_matrix.md`)
+Normative contract: `specs/state.md` §"Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)"
+
+## Goal
+
+Typed public `.orc` runs and fresh Workflow Lisp child frames persist an
+eligible compiler-generated `pure_projection` success as an exact value-free
+completion shell. Resume re-derives the needed pure values in memory from
+durable inputs instead of trusting persisted pure results, bundles or pure
+checkpoints.
+
+## Step order
+
+1. Plan and normative contract (docs only).
+2. `orchestrator/workflow/pure_result_replay.py` import surface; dependency-free
+   constants, `PureResultReplayIndexError` and the profile validator live in
+   `pure_result_replay_core.py` so `orchestrator/state.py` can import them lazily.
+3. `RunState` / `StateManager.initialize` profile field (additive, schema `2.1`).
+4. Replay index derivation (`pure_result_replay_index.py`).
+5. Shell, witness and progress classification (`pure_result_replay_progress.py`).
+6. Atomic `StateManager` / call-frame pure-visit transactions.
+7. `OutcomeRecorder.persist_step_result(..., eligible_pure_settlement=...)`.
+8. Executor forward path: one begin transaction replaces visit increment plus
+   `start_step`; IO-free `evaluate_pure_projection` core; glue in
+   `pure_result_replay_executor.py`.
+9. Checkpoint filtering and the single zero-record `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY`.
+10. Read-only profile preflight and persisted-surface conflict audit
+    (`pure_result_replay_conflicts.py`), before any write.
+11. Replay at resume (`pure_result_replay_runtime.py`).
+12. One restart-boundary determination per resume.
+13. Provider-observation manager created when execution starts.
+14. Automatic selection at roots (`run`, `resume --force-restart`).
+15. Child call-frame selection and `load_existing_call_frame_read_only`.
+16. End-to-end tests (`tests/test_pure_result_replay_e2e.py`).
+17. Verification and status update.
+
+## Assumptions recorded
+
+- Provider-observation lifecycle (step 13) is in scope because the required
+  resume behaviour demands that no observation directory exists before the
+  audit, not because replay needs it.
+- Replay re-derives every `derived_complete` eligible node of the scope (the
+  conservative superset of what the restart boundary needs); only the durable
+  leaves those nodes read are audited.
+- A visitless failed row (a transition-guard or predicate failure recorded
+  before the visit transaction) is not classified as a structural skip; only a
+  visitless `skipped` row for an unselected branch/case descendant is.
+- An eligible pure cursor is left `running` by `fail_run` so an executor
+  exception stays resumable.
+- `PureReplayRuntime.witness_from_state` always yields visit 1; a recorded
+  visit other than 1 is surfaced by classification.
