index 26bd108..9a84c77 100644
--- a/specs/state.md
+++ b/specs/state.md
@@ -592,6 +592,157 @@
 - Resume boundary
   - Because call frames add new durable lineage and resume keys, resume from pre-`schema_version: "2.1"` state is rejected unless a tested upgrader ships with the same tranche.
 
+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+Normative contract for the optional `result_persistence_profile` state field.
+Schema stays `2.1`; the field is additive.
+
+### Selector
+
+- `result_persistence_profile` is optional on the run state (root and call-frame
+  state). Absent means the historical bundle-backed persistence; `to_dict()`
+  omits the key and a payload without it loads as `None` and round-trips
+  unchanged. Loading never infers, backfills, or upgrades the field.
+- The only supported value is `derived_pure_replay.v1`. Any other value fails
+  closed with a `ValueError` mentioning `result_persistence_profile` at
+  `RunState` construction, at `StateManager.initialize(...)`, and on load. A
+  load failure leaves the state file byte-for-byte unchanged.
+- `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=None)` writes the
+  field in the first atomic state write, before any visit. Generic callers stay
+  explicit opt-in.
+
+### Selection
+
+The profile is selected only when new state is created:
+
+- a successfully compiled typed public `.orc` run (`orchestrator run`);
+- the new root created by `orchestrator resume --force-restart` for an `.orc`
+  workflow. The source run is left byte-for-byte unchanged; the requested
+  observability settings are carried only into the new root;
+- a fresh non-iterative child call frame whose callee bundle has
+  `provenance.frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"`. The decision comes from the
+  callee's typed provenance, never from the parent's profile, a path suffix,
+  an alias or a step identity. A fresh retry after a failed non-iterative
+  Workflow Lisp predecessor is new state and selects the profile; the failed
+  predecessor stays unchanged.
+
+Existing roots and frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned child
+frames keep the historical profile. An existing frame is never backfilled. A
+malformed existing frame (no `state`, or a non-mapping `state`) is rejected
+with a `ValueError` mentioning `existing call-frame state` before anything is
+written.
+
+### Eligibility
+
+A pure node is replay-eligible when it is a compiler-generated
+`pure_projection`, is acyclic, is visited at most once per scope and publishes
+no artifacts. Recurrent, loop-owned and other multiply visited pure nodes are
+not eligible (`ineligible_pure_reasons[node_id]`, for example
+`multiple_visit_region`); they keep full durable rows, bundles and
+checkpoints inside a profiled root. Dependencies are the exact
+`{"ref": ...}` leaves of the step's binding documents, scoped to the workflow
+that holds them (an imported callee indexes only its own nodes). Every literal
+leaf must match its declared binding type, including inactive members of union
+literals.
+
+### Value-free completion shell
+
+An eligible pure success is persisted as exactly this row and no other key
+(forbidden examples: `value`, `output`, `text`, `json`, `artifacts`, `debug`,
+`duration_ms`, `output_bundle`):
+
+```json
+{"name": "<presentation_key>", "step_id": "<step_id>", "visit_count": 1,
+ "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0,
+ "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed", "retryable": false},
+ "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}
+```
+
+The full result (with artifacts) lives only in the in-memory state of the
+active executor. Failed and skipped rows stay full durable rows. No pure
+result bundle, `private_artifact_versions` entry, lexical checkpoint record
+(`pending_effect_policy.effect_kind == "pure_projection"`) or restore binding
+sourced from an eligible step is written.
+
+### Visit atomicity and progress table
+
+`StateManager` (and the call-frame manager) expose single-transaction methods:
+`begin_eligible_pure_visit` (visit increment and matching running cursor in one
+write), `reuse_interrupted_eligible_pure_visit` (validates, writes nothing),
+`settle_eligible_pure_success` (shell, cursor cleared) and
+`settle_eligible_pure_failure` (full failed or skipped row, cursor cleared). An
+eligible cursor is not marked `failed` by `fail_run`, so an executor exception
+remains resumable.
+
+For `(step_visits[name], current_step, steps[name])` and a witness of visit 1:
+
+| Class | State |
+| --- | --- |
+| `unstarted` | no visit, no cursor, no row (an unrelated running cursor is allowed) |
+| `interrupted` | visit == witness visit and the matching running cursor `{name, index, type "pure_projection", step_id, visit_count, status "running", started_at, last_heartbeat_at}`; no row |
+| `derived_complete` | visit and the exact shell; no cursor or an unrelated one |
+| `durable_failure_skip` | visit and a full failed/skipped row with matching identity and visit, or the visitless structural skip row written for an unselected branch/case descendant (its name/step id match and no cursor targets it) |
+
+Every other combination is `progress_witness_invalid`: a visit without cursor
+or row; a cursor or shell without a visit; cursor plus row; a visit-two cursor
+or shell; mismatched step id, presentation key, index, type or status; a
+failure or skip with a mismatched visit or identity; a value-bearing
+completion; a non-terminal row.
+
+### Replay at resume
+
+Resume re-derives the values of completed eligible nodes in memory from
+durable inputs (bound inputs, durable intrinsics and non-eligible step rows)
+and installs them only in the executing state view; replay never dispatches an
+effect, increments a visit, settles a result or writes durable state. A resume
+fails closed before any effect with `error.type`
+`pure_result_replay_unavailable` and `error.context.reason`:
+
+| Reason | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `durable_input_missing` / `durable_input_invalid` | required bound input or durable intrinsic (`exit_code`, `outcome.status/phase/class/retryable`) missing or wrongly typed |
+| `binding_unresolved` | re-derivation failed to resolve a ref (`context.cause.type == "materialize_ref_unresolved"`) |
+| `evaluation_failed` | evaluation raised (`cause.type == "pure_evaluation_failed"`) |
+| `output_contract_invalid` | outputs violate the contract (`cause.type == "pure_projection_contract_invalid"`) |
+| `progress_witness_invalid` | see the progress table |
+| `profile_conflict` | see below |
+| `dependency_index_invalid`, `reachability_ambiguous` | the derived dependency index is not well formed |
+
+A union pure result keeps every typed address in the static catalog, but its
+transient row holds exactly the discriminant, the shared outputs and the active
+variant's outputs.
+
+### Persisted-surface conflicts and ordering
+
+A persisted value row (`steps`), pure bundle file (`pure_bundle`), private
+lineage entry (`private_artifact_versions`), same-scope checkpoint record
+(`checkpoint_record`) or restore binding (`restore_payload`) for an eligible
+node is a `profile_conflict` carrying `context.surface`. Noneligible recurrent
+records and other frames' records are allowed. The audit is read-only and runs
+before any state, frame, session, observability or observation-directory
+write (CLI: right after load and checksum validation; executor: before the
+prologue). On rejection source authority (`steps`, `step_visits`,
+`current_step`, `bound_inputs`, frames, checkpoint and bundle files) is
+unchanged; the only write is the single failed-run diagnostic (`status`,
+`error`, `updated_at`).
+
+### Checkpoint filtering and default resume
+
+Replay-eligible points are filtered out of the durable checkpoint candidates
+before unique-nearest selection and emit no record; their derivable pure
+bindings are omitted from restore payloads. Selection never scans past an
+invalid nearest durable boundary: a restorable nearest noneligible point gives
+`selection_reason` `validated_prior_boundary`; otherwise default resume fails
+closed with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`. When no
+durable boundary precedes the restart node, default resume admits exactly one
+zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY` (`mode`
+`LEXICAL_CHECKPOINT_DEFAULT`, `checkpoint_id` null, `selection_reason`
+`validated_frame_entry_replay`), only when the restart node's own selection is
+`record_absent`, the entry prefix is effect-free (every earlier node is an
+eligible pure node that is `derived_complete`/`unstarted`, or an effect node
+with no visit, cursor or row) and bound-input leaves validate. Anything else,
+including a committed command whose checkpoint is missing, fails closed.
+
 ## State File Schema (example)
 
 The state file (`${RUN_ROOT}/state.json`) is the authoritative record of execution:
